              "stem": "Brian is a 40-year-old patient with a previously diagnosed thymus gland disorder who presents with muscle weakness around the eyes (ptosis), as well as generalized muscle fatigue that gets worse with physical exertion. His symptoms are less severe after periods of rest. You suspect that he may have myasthenia gravis. To make a more definitive diagnosis, you run blood tests for elevated antibodies, and administer a drug that will likely produce a rapid transient reversal of his symptoms (e.g. improvement of his ptosis) if he indeed has myasthenia gravis. The drug you administer for your test is:",
