              "modelAnswer": "a) Drug for insomnia: ZOLPIDEM (a non-benzodiazepine hypnotic; a short/intermediate-acting benzodiazepine such as temazepam or zopiclone is an alternative).\n\nb) Mode of action: zolpidem selectively binds the benzodiazepine-1 (BZ1/ω1) site on the GABA-A receptor, allosterically enhancing GABA-mediated Cl- influx (increased frequency of channel opening) → neuronal hyperpolarisation and sedation with minimal muscle-relaxant/anticonvulsant effects. (Benzodiazepines act at the same ω site non-selectively.)\n\nc) Side effects to look out for:\n• Drowsiness, daytime sedation, dizziness, ataxia (especially in the elderly — falls).\n• Anterograde amnesia and cognitive impairment.\n• Tolerance and dependence with prolonged use; rebound insomnia on withdrawal.\n• Bitter/metallic taste (zopiclone), dry mouth.\n• Rarely parasomnias (sleep-walking, sleep-driving), hallucinations.\n• Respiratory depression in susceptible patients (COPD, sleep apnoea)."
