              "stem": "A 71-year-old man with terminal metastatic lung cancer had been hospitalized for 3 months. His renal function had deteriorated, and laboratory results showed serum creatinine 4.5 mg/dL (normal 0.9−1.2 mg/dL) and blood urea nitrogen (BUN) 75 mg/dL (normal 6−20 mg/dL). Because of poor food intake, immobility, and requirement for an opioid analgesia, the patient was severely constipated and required daily laxative therapy. Which of the following would be a suitable laxative for this patient?",
