              "modelAnswer": "CHECKPOINT INHIBITORS (6 marks):\na) THREE CLASSES WITH ONE EXAMPLE EACH:\n1. Anti-CTLA-4 antibodies — Ipilimumab.\n2. Anti-PD-1 antibodies — Nivolumab (or pembrolizumab).\n3. Anti-PD-L1 antibodies — Atezolizumab (or durvalumab, avelumab).\n[These remove the brakes on T cells: CTLA-4 blockade enhances T-cell priming in lymphoid tissue; PD-1/PD-L1 blockade reinvigorates exhausted T cells in the tumor microenvironment → anti-tumor immunity.]\nb) TWO SIDE EFFECTS OF EACH (immune-related adverse events):\n- Ipilimumab: immune-mediated colitis (diarrhea), dermatitis/rash; hepatitis, hypophysitis/endocrinopathies.\n- Nivolumab: pneumonitis, thyroiditis/hypothyroidism; colitis, hepatitis, dermatitis.\n- Atezolizumab: pneumonitis, hepatitis; colitis, fatigue, infusion reactions.\n(Any two per drug.)"
